        <cpr:P3 rdf:resource="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q846"/>
        <cpr:P7 xml:lang="en">Research and development (R&amp;D) investment is the money spent on finding new or improved knowledge and ideas, and applying that knowledge.</cpr:P7>
        <schema:description xml:lang="en">Research and development (R&amp;D) investment is the money spent on finding new or improved knowledge and ideas, and applying that knowledge.</schema:description>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q1336 -->


    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q1336">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">individual transferable quota</rdfs:label>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">individual transferable quotas, ITQ, ITQs, tradable development right, tradable development rights, tradable fishing right, tradable fishing rights, tradable hunting right, tradable hunting rights, tradable quota, transferable fishing quota, transferable fishing quotas, transferable hunting quota, transferable hunting quotas</skos:altLabel>
        <cpr:P2 rdf:resource="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q1280"/>
        <cpr:P7 xml:lang="en">Includes individual transferable quotas (ITQs) for fisheries, tradable development rights, and tradable hunting rights. These policy instruments set a limit on the total amount of a natural resource that can be exploited, and then allocate individual permits to users that they can also trade.</cpr:P7>
        <schema:description xml:lang="en">These policy instruments set a limit on the total amount of a natural resource that can be exploited, and then allocate individual permits to users that they can also trade.</schema:description>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q1372 -->


    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q1372">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">baseline and credit system</rdfs:label>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">baseline and credit system, baseline and credit systems, baseline-and-credit system, baseline-and-credit systems</skos:altLabel>
        <cpr:P2 rdf:resource="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q1374"/>
        <cpr:P7 xml:lang="en">Under a baseline-and-credit system, there is no fixed limit on emissions, but polluters that reduce their emissions beyond their obligation can earn “credits” to sell to other polluters who need them in order to comply with regulations.</cpr:P7>
        <schema:description xml:lang="en">Under a baseline-and-credit system, there is no fixed limit on emissions, but polluters that reduce their emissions beyond their obligation can earn “credits” to sell to other polluters who need them in order to comply with regulations.</schema:description>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q1373 -->


    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q1373">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">green certificate</rdfs:label>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">green certificates, REC</skos:altLabel>
        <cpr:P2 rdf:resource="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q1280"/>
        <cpr:P7 xml:lang="en">A certificate in which the commodity (i.e. permit) represents a fixed amount of electricity from renewables that can be traded in order to comply with renewable energy quotas established by the government. Governments can use this renewable energy policy instrument to set targets for renewable energy production.</cpr:P7>
        <schema:description xml:lang="en">A certificate in which the commodity (i.e. permit) represents a fixed amount of electricity from renewables that can be traded in order to comply with renewable energy quotas established by the government.</schema:description>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q1374 -->


    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q1374">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">offset scheme</rdfs:label>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">biodiversity offset, offsetting scheme, tradable offset, tradable offsets, climate offset, climate offsets, offset credit, offset credits, offset payment, offset payments, offset schemes, biodiversity offsets</skos:altLabel>
        <cpr:P1 rdf:resource="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q1372"/>
        <cpr:P1 rdf:resource="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q1375"/>
        <cpr:P2 rdf:resource="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q1280"/>
        <cpr:P7 xml:lang="en">Tradable permits can also take the form of offsets, such as biodiversity offsets, which are intended for polluters to compensate for the adverse impacts of an activity (e.g. land conversion) on biodiversity services or carbon emissions.</cpr:P7>
        <schema:description xml:lang="en">Tradable permits can also take the form of offsets, such as biodiversity offsets, which are intended for polluters to compensate for the adverse impacts of an activity (e.g. land conversion) on biodiversity services or carbon emissions.</schema:description>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q1375 -->


    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q1375">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">carbon offset</rdfs:label>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">carbon offsetting, carbon offsets, carbon offset project, carbon offset projects, carbon offset scheme, carbon-offset, offset carbon policy, offset emissions</skos:altLabel>
        <cpr:P2 rdf:resource="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q1374"/>
        <cpr:P7 xml:lang="en">A voluntary market where individuals and businesses can purchase certificates to fund projects that reduce carbon emissions. These carbon offsets are traded by corporations, individuals and organizations that are under no legal obligation to make emission cuts.</cpr:P7>
        <schema:description xml:lang="en">A voluntary market where individuals and businesses can purchase certificates to fund projects that reduce carbon emissions.</schema:description>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q1376 -->


    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q1376">
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">payment for ecosystem services</rdfs:label>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">payment for ecosystem service, payment for ecosystem services, PES, agri-environmental payment, agri-environmental payments, environmental payment, environmental payments, environmental compensation payment, environmental compensation payments, payment for environmental services, environmental services payments, payment for ecosystems services</skos:altLabel>
        <cpr:P2 rdf:resource="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q1274"/>
        <cpr:P2 rdf:resource="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q1836"/>
        <cpr:P2 rdf:resource="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q1846"/>
        <cpr:P7 xml:lang="en">Policies that provide compensation for undertaking certain actions, such as those which increase the provision of ecosystem services. These payments can be made and received by the private sector, whereby the government acts as an intermediary.</cpr:P7>
        <schema:description xml:lang="en">Policies that provide compensation for undertaking certain actions, such as those which increase the provision of ecosystem services. These payments can be made and received by the private sector, whereby the government acts as an intermediary.</schema:description>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q1378 -->


    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q1378">
