        <cpr:P2 rdf:resource="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q1430"/>
        <cpr:P7 xml:lang="en">PPC permits are regulatory requirements for industries that may release pollutants. These permits cover energy activities like combustion and refining, metals production, and mineral processing such as cement, lime, glass, and ceramics manufacturing. They ensure compliance with environmental standards to protect air, water, and land quality, reducing harm to public health and ecosystems.</cpr:P7>
        <schema:description xml:lang="en">Pollution prevention and control permits are required for industrial activities that may pollute, like energy production, metals processing, and mineral manufacturing to protect the environment.</schema:description>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


