        <cpr:P2 rdf:resource="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q1281"/>
        <cpr:P7 xml:lang="en">Environmental standards are legal tools used by governments to limit pollution and enforce climate action. They set thresholds for air, water, emissions, and waste, ensuring industries comply. Examples include air quality limits, emissions caps, and energy efficiency rules, promoting sustainability.</cpr:P7>
        <schema:description xml:lang="en">Environmental standards are legal tools used by governments to limit pollution and enforce climate action. They set thresholds for air, water, emissions, and waste, ensuring industries comply. Examples include air quality limits, emissions caps, and energy efficiency rules, promoting sustainability.</schema:description>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


